st_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": 1000000, "model_max_tokens": 128000, "output_tail": "Adding a regression test, then running it.\n`round_money(2.675)` now returns `2.68`.\n\n**Cause:** 2.675 can't be stored exactly as a binary float; Python keeps it as 2.67499999\u2026, so the built-in `round(x, 2)` rounds it down. `round()` also sends exact halves to the even digit (`round(0.125, 2)` gives `0.12`), so it never did the \"half up\" rounding the docstring promises.\n\n**Fix** in `pricing/money.py`: `round_money` now turns the number into text with `str(x)`, which gives the short form a person would write (`\"2.675\"`). It then rounds that to cents with `Decimal`, always taking halves up, and returns a float as before. `add_vat` uses `round_money`, so it gets the fix too.\n\n**Test:** I added `tests/test_round_money.py`, covering 2.675 \u2192 2.68, 1.005 \u2192 1.01, 0.125 \u2192 0.13, -2.675 \u2192 -2.68 and 2.674 \u2192 2.67. pytest isn't installed here, so I called the test functions directly with `python3`. Both new tests and the existing `test_split` pass, and the built-in `round` gives `2.67` and `0.12` on the same inputs, confirming the bug.\n\nNegative halves now round away from zero (-2.675 \u2192 -2.68).", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 2, "replies_ok": 10, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 282750, "requests_cache_write": 8755, "requests_cost_usd": 0.14511300000000002, "requests_count": 10, "requests_input_uncached": 22, "requests_output": 2235, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-bugfix-regress:claude-opus-5-5:trial25", "run_seed": 20261014, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 49, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-13T06:18:54.352238+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 29.664, "t_checker_s": 0.379, "t_env_setup_s": 0.001, "